0:{"rsc":["$","$1","c",{"children":[[["$","$L2","2.9",{"topic":{"id":"2.9","title":"Admissibility of Electronic Evidence","minutes":15,"summary":"An electronic file can be relevant and still require a proper route to proof. Separate admissibility, authenticity, and weight.","sections":[{"title":"The route from record to document","body":["BSA section 57 includes electronic or digital records within documentary evidence. Section 61 addresses legal recognition of electronic records. Section 62 requires proof of electronic-record contents in accordance with section 63. Section 63 treats qualifying computer or communication-device output as a document when its conditions are satisfied. These provisions work together rather than as interchangeable slogans.","Distinguish the original electronic record from a printout, copied file, or other output. Section 63 addresses regular use, lawful control, ordinary input or derivation, and proper operation of the relevant device or combination of devices. A network, cloud service, or multiple-device process may require facts beyond the single handset in the witness box."]},{"title":"Precedent and the current certificate","body":["Anvar held that the special electronic-record proof route in section 65B displaced the general secondary-evidence route for the output concerned. Arjun clarified the certificate position and disapproved the relaxation in Shafhi Mohammad. It also explained that production of the original device itself is a different situation from tendering a copy or output. These holdings must now be read with the BSA’s text.","For an output under BSA section 63, subsection (4) calls for a certificate at each instance of submission for admission, signed by the relevant person in charge and an expert, in the Schedule’s form. The Schedule includes Part A and Part B, source particulars, and hash information. Do not reuse an old one-signature section 65B template without checking the new requirements."]},{"title":"Admissible does not mean conclusive","body":["Authentication, hearsay, relevance, privilege, and the manner of collection may raise separate issues. A certified chat can still contain a false statement or be misattributed. The court evaluates the evidence in context, including corroboration and the witness’s ability to explain the process. A certificate is not a declaration that every statement in the file is true.","Prepare the source witness, device custodian, and expert with accurate roles. Keep the original or reliable source available where lawful, preserve the full conversation, and disclose material limitations. The certificate builder in this course is a training worksheet, not a signed legal certificate or a guarantee of admissibility."]}],"practice":{"title":"The original-phone question","scenario":"A party proposes to bring the original phone to court rather than only submitting a chat printout.","steps":["Identify the precise record and the form in which it will be tendered.","Read BSA sections 61–63 and the Arjun clarification.","Separate original-device production from proof of copied output.","List the facts and signatures needed for the actual submission route."],"debrief":"Do not answer “every phone needs a certificate” or “a screenshot never needs one” in the abstract. Identify the output, statutory route, and applicable precedent."},"terms":[],"lawIds":["bsa","iea"],"sources":["bsa","bsa-schedule","anvar","arjun"],"labId":"certificate","unit":2,"objectives":["Explain the route from record to document and apply it to an investigation.","Explain precedent and the current certificate and apply it to an investigation.","Explain admissible does not mean conclusive and apply it to an investigation."],"question":{"id":"q-2.9","prompt":"Which distinction is most important when discussing electronic evidence?","options":["File size versus screen size.","Admissibility versus truth and evidential weight.","Laptop brand versus phone brand.","Internet speed versus download speed."],"answer":1,"explanation":"A record may be admitted yet still be unreliable, false, or insufficient to prove the allegation.","unit":2}}}]],["$L3"],"$L4"]}],"isPartial":false,"staleTime":300,"varyParams":null,"buildId":"mMiCr23A_-Cpk0hZkfT7X"}
